  "goodToKnow": "Die Meile is a mile. Germany uses kilometres, so Meilen appear mostly for the US and UK, at sea (die Seemeile, nautical mile) and in idioms: Das riecht man drei Meilen gegen den Wind (you can tell from a mile away). Der Meilenstein is a milestone. Die Fanmeile is the public viewing area for big football tournaments, like the one in Berlin by the Brandenburg Gate. From Latin mille (thousand paces)."
